# UI test: a `tool` with no body (SC0198).
#
# There is no abstract tool. A signature with no body is an interface's
# required method, and that is declared with `def`.
#
# The neighbouring case this must not become: a `tool` whose body is indented
# with no `:` in front of it already reports the missing colon, and reporting
# that the body is absent as well would be a second true statement about one
# mistake. The check is on the one branch where nothing has been said yet.

## Fit peaks in a time-of-flight window.
tool fit_peaks(window_lower: F64) -> Int
